  // Trusted libraries: "library" is the allowlist name. Curated against the allowlist the index
  // was run with (StarMap 0.4.6 to 0.5.2, Oxidizer 0.1.0 to 0.6.1).
  "libraries": {
    "exempt": [
      // Harmony's patching API. Patching is code generation (the replacement method is built
      // with Emit and loaded as an in-memory assembly), native code and raw memory (a jump is
      // written over the original's compiled code) and reflection on the originals and patch
      // methods the mod hands over. What is patched, and with what, is accounted for at the mod:
      // the patch methods are mod code; a HarmonyMethod or PatchProcessor.Add* target must be
      // traced to a name (reflection provenance), and [HarmonyPatch] attribute targets are decoded
      // from the mod. Every mod calling it still gets "Changes how the game works". Running a mod's
      // transpilers is part of patching ("code-rewrite" is exempt here); the transpiler helpers
      // (CodeInstruction, CodeMatcher, Transpilers) are not exempt, so a mod using them is code-rewrite.
      // What a mod's transpiler rewrites is placed at the mod ("rewrite-outside-game" is exempt here:
      // inside, Harmony adds the transpilers it is given to originals it is given).
